@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@eventId = REPLACE_WITH_EVENT_ID
@mlUrl = http://localhost:8001

### 1. Health and database connection status
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Create a clearly labelled demo event
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attackType": "Ransomware",
  "targetAsset": "Critical Database Server",
  "eventFrequency": 85,
  "assetCriticality": 95,
  "vulnerabilityContext": 80,
  "sourceReputation": 90,
  "historicalOccurrence": 70,
  "potentialImpact": 98,
  "affectedScope": 75,
  "description": "Illustrative demo event",
  "dataMode": "Demo"
}

### 3. Retrieve all events
GET {{baseUrl}}/events

### 4. Retrieve one event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}

### Analyze an event (creates one demo prediction and one alert; repeat calls reuse it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/analyze

### 5. Filter by attack type
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?attackType=Ransomware

### 6. Create an asset
POST {{baseUrl}}/assets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Critical Database Server",
  "assetType": "Database Server",
  "criticality": 95,
  "owner": "Infrastructure Team"
}

### 7. Retrieve assets
GET {{baseUrl}}/assets

### 8. Invalid event input
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attackType": "Invalid Attack",
  "targetAsset": "",
  "eventFrequency": 101
}

### 9. Nonexistent event
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/000000000000000000000000

### ML service health
GET {{mlUrl}}/health

### Direct demo rule-based risk score
POST {{mlUrl}}/predict/risk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attackType": "Ransomware",
  "eventFrequency": 85,
  "assetCriticality": 95,
  "vulnerabilityContext": 80,
  "sourceReputation": 90,
  "historicalOccurrence": 70,
  "potentialImpact": 98,
  "affectedScope": 75
}

### Future attack-detection contract: returns 503 until a trained model exists
POST {{mlUrl}}/predict/attack
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flowSchema": "CIC-IDS2017",
  "flowFeatures": {
    "Flow Duration": 1000,
    "Total Fwd Packets": 10
  }
}
